From: System Electronics
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 16:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: hailo15-isp: route MCM input to the CSI1 context

The upstream MCM input group is hardcoded to VDID 0. Astrial H15 carries
its camera on CSI1 and therefore consumes the ISP output through VDID 1.
Pre-ISP AI denoise captures the CSI1 raw stream correctly, but reinjects
the processed buffers into VDID 0, so no frame reaches the CSI1 ISP output.

Route MCM input through VDID 1 for the Astrial camera topology.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Astrial H15 board-specific camera topology]

---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/hailo/hailo15/common.h b/drivers/media/platform/hailo/hailo15/common.h
--- a/drivers/media/platform/hailo/hailo15/common.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/hailo/hailo15/common.h
@@ -716,9 +716,7 @@ static inline uint8_t HAILO15_VID_GRP_TO_VDID(int grp_id)
 	case HAILO15_VID_GRP_SX_CSI1_ISP_SP:
 		return 1;
 	case HAILO15_VID_GRP_MCM_IN:
-		// currently MCM-IN path is only in use
-		// for VDID 0.
-		return 0;
+		return 1;
 	default:
 		return VIV_INVALID_VDID;
 	}
